{"format":1,"kind":"nrl","id":"nrl-sl-1997","version":"nrl-sl-1997-e986d79b","year":1997,"season":"1997","label":"Super League (computed)","local":false,"source":{"provider":"Rugby League Project","edition":"Rugby League Project, the 1997 Super League premiership","compiler":"computed by imperialism-game from the Rugby League Project's season lists (who started, where and how often, his tries), results and representative sides","url":"https://www.rugbyleagueproject.org/seasons/super-league-1997/players.html","retrieved":"2026-11-14","method":"computed","metric":"selections (club starts and representative games) and tries a club game, the previous season at half weight","conversion":"Players: everyone the Rugby League Project lists as taking the field in the Super League's 1997 premiership, its finals included; his club the one he played most games for (of two as many, the first RLP lists). Position: the one he started at most that season (RLP's starts by position; the bench is no start), else in the seasons either side, then two either side; else he is left out. Value: his selections, the games he started for his club and his representative games (Tests, State of Origin or the interstate series, NSW City v Country), plus 2 for each try at today's 4 tries a team game, scaled to his season's rate (`tryRate`), per club game, the season before at half weight when he played in it. Overall: the value's mid-rank percentile among the season's players at his position, read off Rugby League 26's overalls at that position by as many of each 2025 club's best as the season's clubs carry per club (`quota`), by linear interpolation; rounded and held to 1-99. Club shift: the season's results set each club's level and how far apart the clubs play, while its players keep their order. Each club's Simple Rating System (`srs`), its regular season's margins adjusted for its opponents and a home edge by least squares, is scaled to the clubs' own spread, times the square root of the rating